This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - **Active task (carried from prior session)**: "本地的这个「怎么访问我的 boe 机器」tab 好像切换起来还是很慢" — the session tab titled "怎么访问我的 boe 机器" is STILL slow to switch to, despite the P0+P1 markdown rendering fix from the prior session. Investigate and fix.
   - **Root cause (confirmed in prior session, verified this session)**: GET /api/sessions/[id] returns 10.26MB payload, 98.6% of which is toolCalls JSON (10.12MB); response text only 0.09MB. Payload refetched on EVERY tab switch (no caching). Gate (server.ts) strips compression via passthroughHeaders. On-box processing ~190ms is fast; the user's remote Mac browser pays the full 10.26MB transfer.
   - **Fix approach chosen and implemented**: Lazy toolCalls — strip toolCalls from session payload, ship precomputed `toolCallStats` + `generatedFiles` for badges/bars; add GET /api/nodes/[id]/tool-calls endpoint for on-demand loading when the ToolTimeline is expanded. Streaming path unchanged (toolCalls arrive via stream events).
   - Standing constraints: default Chinese communication; progress protocol mandatory after code changes (sessions.md new entry + rotate oldest of >5 into archive.md in same round; README Current Focus one sentence ≤200 chars); commit/push only when user asks; 飞书/Lark write operations require reading `~/.claude/skills/lark-shared/references/write-gates.md` + literal user confirmation first; AGENTS.md: this is a modified Next.js — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing Next.js code; untracked files NOT mine — do not touch/commit: RELEASE.json, modelhub-proxy.js, modelhub-proxy.log.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Trellis: Next.js 16.2.4 (Turbopack, modified), bun 1.3.14, bun:sqlite, zustand, React Flow (@xyflow/react v12), react-markdown v10.1.0, dagre layout
   - Architecture: gate (server.ts, bun) on :3088 → spawns Next on :3187; gate handles auth cookie, proxies all requests
   - Auth gate: `trellis_auth` cookie = TRELLIS_AUTH_TOKEN; gateOn = Boolean(TRELLIS_AUTH_PASS && TRELLIS_AUTH_TOKEN); token in `/data00/home/zhangpeng.pada/.trellis/shared/.env.local`
   - DB path: `/data00/home/zhangpeng.pada/.trellis/data.db`; overridable via `TRELLIS_DB_PATH` env var (lib/server/sqlite.ts:14)
   - BOE session ID: `37f1e158-bfe2-4564-b49a-45767900d964` (91 nodes)
   - tool-tree.ts functions (client-safe, type-only imports): buildToolTree, countToolTree (returns ToolTreeCounts {total, subagents, workflows, errors}), walkToolTree, subagentLabel
   - Dev server cannot run via `next dev` because bun:sqlite is unavailable in Node context; project runs under Bun (`bun server.ts` for prod)
   - S98 deployment lesson: `HOME=/data00/home/zhangpeng.pada make deploy` (devbox HOME is a symlink that breaks Turbopack)

3. Files and Code Sections:
   - **lib/types.ts** (modified)
     - Added ToolCallStats and GeneratedFile types after ToolCall (~line 163):
       ```ts
       export type ToolCallStats = {
         total: number;
         subagents: number;
         workflows: number;
         errors: number;
         labels: string[];
       };
       export type GeneratedFile = { absPath: string; name: string };
       ```
     - ChatNode.toolCalls comment expanded; added two optional fields after toolCalls:
       ```ts
       toolCallStats?: ToolCallStats | null;
       generatedFiles?: GeneratedFile[];
       ```
   - **lib/generated-files.ts** (modified)
     - Changed import to `import type { ChatNode, GeneratedFile, ToolCall } from "./types";` + `export type { GeneratedFile };`
     - Refactored core logic to `generatedFilesFromToolCalls(toolCalls: ToolCall[]): GeneratedFile[]` (extracted from generatedFilesFromNode); kept `generatedFilesFromNode(node)` as wrapper calling it. WRITE_TOOLS = Write/Edit/MultiEdit/NotebookEdit.
   - **app/api/sessions/[id]/route.ts** (modified)
     - Added imports: buildToolTree, countToolTree, subagentLabel, walkToolTree from "@/lib/tool-tree"; generatedFilesFromToolCalls from "@/lib/generated-files"
     - GET handler now strips toolCalls and adds stats:
       ```ts
       const slimNodes = nodes.map((n) => {
         const tree = buildToolTree(n.toolCalls);
         const counts = countToolTree(tree);
         const labels = walkToolTree(tree)
           .filter((t) => t.kind === "subagent")
           .map((t) => subagentLabel(t.meta));
         return {
           ...n,
           // toolCalls 占载荷 98%（实测 10.12MB / 10.26MB），不下发——
           // JSON.stringify 会丢弃 undefined 字段。客户端按需走
