   Immediately before the summary request, I was attempting end-to-end verification of the lazy toolCalls fix. The dev server could not run (bun:sqlite unavailable under Node `next dev`). A measurement script importing repo.ts triggered a migration failure against the prod DB: `SQLiteError: table cli_lineages has no column named claude_session_id` at sqlite.ts:234. I investigated and confirmed this is a PRE-EXISTING schema mismatch on main (prod DB has old `cli_lineages` with `cli_session_id` + `provider_family` columns; current main code renamed to `claude_session_id` but the migration's CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS is a no-op on the existing table, so the INSERT fails). The table is empty (0 rows). I then read lib/server/sqlite.ts lines 1-40 and found `dbPath()` returns `process.env.TRELLIS_DB_PATH || DB_PATH` (line 14), planning to copy the prod DB to /tmp, fix the cli_lineages schema in the copy, and run the route logic against the copy via TRELLIS_DB_PATH to verify my changes without touching prod. All code changes are complete and pass tsc + eslint; only end-to-end verification and progress-protocol documentation remain.

